lustering at the player or referee level", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["standard errors", "clustering"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [100, 101]}, {"id": 100, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[118, 118]], "assertion": "the median number of dyads per player is about 73, and per referee about 39", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["clustering"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [99, 101]}, {"id": 101, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[118, 118]], "assertion": "this clustering likely underestimates standard errors, making p-values anticonservative, though this does not change the main conclusion since the primary result was already non-significant", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["standard errors", "p-values"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [99, 100]}, {"id": 102, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[119, 119]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 103, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[120, 120]], "note": "Risk Difference Calculation subheading"}, {"id": 104, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[121, 128]], "assertion": "the risk difference was calculated via marginal standardization: fitting the logistic model, creating counterfactual datasets with skin_dark set to 1 and to 0, predicting probabilities, and differencing the mean predicted probabilities", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["risk difference", "marginal standardization"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 105, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[129, 129]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 106, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[130, 130]], "assertion": "this approach is said to provide a population-average causal estimate under the assumption that all confounders are controlled for", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["marginal standardization", "causal estimate"], "confidence": "medium"}, {"id": 107, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[131, 133]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 108, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[134, 135]], "note": "Conclusion heading"}, {"id": 109, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[136, 136]], "assertion": "the hypothesis is NOT SUPPORTED by the primary analysis", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["hypothesis"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 110, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[137, 137]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 111, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[138, 138]], "note": "Evidence for this conclusion subheading"}, {"id": 112, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[139, 139]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 113, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[140, 140]], "assertion": "the effect size is very small (0.11pp), less than a 10% relative increase over the baseline risk of about 1.2%", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect size"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 114, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[141, 141]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 115, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[142, 142]], "assertion": "the 95% CI [-0.07, 0.31] includes zero and the p-value (0.236) is above the 0.05 threshold", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confidence interval", "p-value"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 116, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[143, 143]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 117, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[144, 144]], "assertion": "even the upper bound of the confidence interval implies limited practical significance (text appears truncated/garbled at this point)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["practical significance"], "confidence": "low"}, {"id": 118, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[145, 145]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 119, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[146, 146]], "assertion": "sensitivity analyses suggest a possible dose-response relationship between darker skin tone and higher red-card rates, though small and only detectable at extremes or when treating skin tone as continuous", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["dose-response", "skin tone"], "confidence": "low"}, {"id": 120, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[147, 147]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 121, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[148, 148]], "note": "label 'Possible interpretations:'"}, {"id": 122, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[149, 149]], "assertion": "one possible interpretation is that no true effect exists and the sensitivity-analysis findings are false positives", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["interpretation"], "confidence": "low"}, {"id": 123, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[150, 150]], "assertion": "another possible interpretation is that a small true effect exists, detectable only with the greater power of extreme-group contrasts", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["interpretation"], "confidence": "low"}, {"id": 124, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[151, 151]], "assertion": "another possible interpretation is a non-linear relationship with effects concentrated at the darkest skin tones", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["interpretation"], "confidence": "low"}, {"id": 125, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[152, 154]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 126, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[155, 156]], "note": "Limitations and Sources of Bias heading"}, {"id": 127, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[157, 157]], "note": "Data Structure and Clustering subheading"}, {"id": 128, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[158, 158]], "assertion": "the analysis treats dyads as independent even though the same players and referees appear in multiple dyads, violating the independence assumption", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["independence assumption", "clustering"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 129, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[159, 159]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 130, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[160, 160]], "assertion": "standard errors are likely underestimated, making p-values anticonservative, but since the primary analysis was non-significant this would only strengthen the null conclusion", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["standard errors", "p-values"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [131]}, {"id": 131, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[160, 160]], "assertion": "using clustered standard errors would likely produce a larger p-value", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["standard errors"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": [130]}, {"id": 132, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[161, 161]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 133, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[162, 162]], "assertion": "a player-level cluster bootstrap was attempted but abandoned as computationally infeasible (over 10 minutes for 2000 iterations); future work is recommended to use mixed-effects models or cluster-robust standard errors instead", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["cluster bootstrap", "standard errors"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 134, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[163, 163]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 135, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[164, 164]], "note": "Selection Bias subheading"}, {"id": 136, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[165, 165]], "assertion": "20.8% of dyads were excluded due to missing data, including 14.7% for missing skin-tone ratings caused by unavailable player photos", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["exclusions", "skin tone ratings"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [137]}, {"id": 137, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[165, 165]], "assertion": "missing-photo exclusions may introduce selection bias if photo availability relates to both skin tone and red-card risk", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["selection bias"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": [136]}, {"id": 138, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[166, 166]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 139, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[167, 167]], "assertion": "players without photos may be less prominent or play fewer games", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["selection bias"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": [140]}, {"id": 140, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[167, 167]], "assertion": "the codebook indicates 1,586 of 2,053 players (77%) had photos available, indicating substantial exclusions", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["photo availability"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [139]}, {"id": 141, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[168, 168]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 142, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[169, 169]], "note": "states the direction of possible selection bias is unknown, no specific action asserted"}, {"id": 143, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[170, 170]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 144, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[171, 171]], "note": "Confounding subheading"}, {"id": 145, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[172, 172]], "note": "intro sentence to list of unmeasured confounders"}, {"id": 146, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[173, 173]], "assertion": "playing style/aggression was not measured as a potential confounder", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["playing style", "confounding"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 147, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[174, 174]], "assertion": "referee race/ethnicity was not available (anonymized); bias measures exist only at the country level, not per individual referee", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["referee characteristics", "confounding"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 148, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[175, 175]], "assertion": "match context (game importance, score differential, home/away status) was not controlled for", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["match context", "confounding"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 149, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[176, 176]], "assertion": "player reputation / prior disciplinary history was not available or controlled for", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["player reputation", "confounding"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 150, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[177, 177]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 151, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[178, 178]], "note": "generic statement that confounding could bias in either direction, no specific action asserted"}, {"id": 152, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[179, 179]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 153, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[180, 180]], "note": "Measurement Error subheading"}, {"id": 154, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[181, 181]], "assertion": "skin tone was coded from static profile photos, which may not reflect in-game appearance due to lighting, angle, or image-quality differences", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["skin tone measurement"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [155]}, {"id": 155, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[181, 181]], "assertion": "despite excellent inter-rater reliability (r=0.923), the validity of the skin-tone measure is unknown", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["skin tone measurement", "validity"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": [154]}, {"id": 156, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[182, 182]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 157, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[183, 183]], "assertion": "non-differential measurement error in the binary skin-tone exposure would bias estimates toward the null", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["measurement error"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": [158]}, {"id": 158, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[183, 183]], "assertion": "this may explain why the dichotomous analysis found no effect while the continuous analysis did", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["measurement error", "dose-response"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": [157]}, {"id": 159, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[184, 184]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 160, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[185, 185]], "note": "Multiple Testing subheading"}, {"id": 161, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[186, 186]], "assertion": "multiple model specifications and sensitivity analyses were conducted without formal adjustment for multiple comparisons", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["multiple testing"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 162, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[187, 187]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 163, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[188, 188]], "assertion": "the significant sensitivity-analysis findings (p=0.009, p=0.017) may be false positives due to increased Type I error risk from multiple testing", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["multiple testing", "false positives"], "confidence": "low"}, {"id": 164, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[189, 189]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 165, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[190, 190]], "note": "Rare Outcome subheading"}, {"id": 166, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[191, 191]], "assertion": "only 1.26% of dyads had red cards; the low event rate reduces statistical power and may cause sparse-data bias", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["rare outcome"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 167, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[192, 192]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 168, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[193, 193]], "assertion": "with 115,603 dyads and 1,455 events, the events-per-parameter rule of thumb (10 EPV) is satisfied (121 events per parameter)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sample size", "rare outcome"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 169, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[194, 194]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 170, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[195, 195]], "note": "Collider Bias subheading"}, {"id": 171, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[196, 196]], "assertion": "adjusting for games played could induce collider bias if games played is affected by both skin tone and red-card propensity", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["collider bias", "games played"], "confidence": "low"}, {"id": 172, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[197, 197]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 173, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[198, 198]], "assertion": "games played is unlikely to be a strong collider since it primarily reflects career length and selection rather than consequences of red cards", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["collider bias"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [174]}, {"id": 174, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[198, 198]], "assertion": "a sensitivity analysis without adjusting for games showed similar results", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sensitivity analysis", "games played"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [173]}, {"id": 175, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[199, 199]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 176, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[200, 200]], "note": "Key Assumption Not Met: Independence subheading"}, {"id": 177, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[201, 201]], "assertion": "the independence assumption is clearly violated because dyads are clustered within players and referees", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["independence assumption"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [178, 179]}, {"id": 178, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[201, 201]], "assertion": "an attempt was made to address clustering via bootstrap, but computational constraints prevented full implementation", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["cluster bootstrap"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [177, 179]}, {"id": 179, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[201, 201]], "assertion": "this unaddressed clustering is characterized as the most serious limitation of the analysis", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["limitations"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [177, 178]}, {"id": 180, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[202, 204]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 181, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[205, 206]], "note": "Supplementary Analyses heading"}, {"id": 182, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[207, 207]], "note": "Model Comparison subheading"}, {"id": 183, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[208, 208]], "assertion": "three logistic regression models were fit with increasing levels of covariate adjustment", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["model comparison"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 184, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[209, 209]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 185, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[210, 211]], "note": "table header row"}, {"id": 186, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[212, 212]], "assertion": "the unadjusted model gives OR=1.049 (95% CI 0.912-1.206), p=0.505", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["model 1"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 187, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[213, 213]], "assertion": "the model adjusted for position, league, and games gives OR=1.100 (95% CI 0.949-1.276), p=0.206", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["model 2"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 188, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[214, 214]], "assertion": "the fully adjusted model gives OR=1.095 (95% CI 0.943-1.271), p=0.232", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["model 3"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 189, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[215, 215]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 190, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[216, 216]], "assertion": "adjusting for covariates slightly increased the point estimate but did not materially change the conclusions", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["model comparison"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [191]}, {"id": 191, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[216, 216]], "assertion": "the unadjusted analysis also showed no significant effect", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["model 1"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [190]}, {"id": 192, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[217, 217]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 193, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[218, 218]], "note": "Descriptive Statistics by Skin Tone subheading"}, {"id": 194, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[219, 219]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 195, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[220, 221]], "note": "table header row"}, {"id": 196, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[222, 222]], "assertion": "N dyads is 97,425 for light skin and 18,178 for dark skin", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["descriptive stats"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 197, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[223, 223]], "assertion": "red card rate is 1.25% for light skin and 1.31% for dark skin", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["descriptive stats"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 198, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[224, 224]], "assertion": "mean games per dyad is 3.05 for light skin and 2.96 for dark skin", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["descriptive stats"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 199, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[225, 225]], "assertion": "mean player age is 28.3 for light skin and 27.9 for dark skin", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["descriptive stats"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 200, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[226, 226]], "assertion": "mean player height is 182.3cm for light skin and 181.7cm for dark skin", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["descriptive stats"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 201, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[227, 227]], "assertion": "mean player weight is 76.6kg for light skin and 76.2kg for dark skin", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["descriptive stats"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 202, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[228, 228]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 203, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[229, 229]], "assertion": "the unadjusted risk difference is 0.06 percentage points (1.31%-1.25%)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["unadjusted risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [204]}, {"id": 204, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[229, 229]], "assertion": "this is smaller than the adjusted estimate, suggesting modest positive confounding", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confounding"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": [203]}, {"id": 205, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[230, 232]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 206, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[233, 234]], "note": "Reproducibility heading"}, {"id": 207, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[235, 235]], "assertion": "the complete analysis code was saved to /workspace/final_analysis.py and can be re-run to reproduce all results", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["analysis code", "reproducibility"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [208]}, {"id": 208, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[235, 237]], "assertion": "two figures were generated: a descriptive plot (skin-tone distribution, red-card rates by skin tone/position/league) and a forest plot of odds ratios from the three models", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["figures"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [207]}, {"id": 209, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[238, 238]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 210, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[239, 239]], "note": "label 'Software versions:'"}, {"id": 211, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[240, 240]], "assertion": "Python 3.11 was used", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["software"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 212, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[241, 241]], "assertion": "pandas 2.x was used", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["software"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 213, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[242, 242]], "assertion": "statsmodels (version from environment) was used", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["software"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 214, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[243, 243]], "assertion": "numpy, scipy, matplotlib, and seaborn were used", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["software"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 215, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[244, 244]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 216, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[245, 245]], "assertion": "the random seed was set to 42 for the confidence interval simulation", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["random seed"], "confidence": "high"}, {"id": 217, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[246, 248]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 218, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[249, 250]], "note": "Recommendations for Future Research heading"}, {"id": 219, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[251, 258]], "note": "list of recommendations for future research; forward-looking advice, not a claim about what this analysis did or found"}, {"id": 220, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[259, 261]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 221, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[262, 263]], "note": "Final Statement heading"}, {"id": 222, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[264, 264]], "assertion": "based on the analysis of 115,603 dyads using fully adjusted logistic regression and marginal standardization, the hypothesis that referees favor red cards for dark-skinned players is NOT SUPPORTED", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["hypothesis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [223]}, {"id": 223, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[264, 264]], "assertion": "the adjusted risk difference is 0.11 percentage points (95% CI -0.07 to 0.31; p=0.236), very small, not statistically significant, and consistent with no effect", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [222]}, {"id": 224, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[265, 265]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 225, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[266, 266]], "assertion": "sensitivity analyses treating skin tone as continuous or comparing extreme groups reveal small but statistically significant associations, suggesting the relationship depends on how skin tone is operationalized", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sensitivity analyses", "skin tone"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [226]}, {"id": 226, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[266, 266]], "assertion": "the clinical/practical significance of these effects is questionable given the very small absolute probability differences (about 0.2-0.3 percentage points)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["practical significance"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": [225]}, {"id": 227, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[267, 267]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 228, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[268, 268]], "assertion": "the analysis has important limitations, particularly failing to account for clustering within players and referees, which likely leads to anticonservative inference", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["clustering", "limitations"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [229]}, {"id": 229, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[268, 268]], "assertion": "despite this, the primary finding of no significant effect is robust across multiple model specifications and is unlikely to change with proper clustering adjustment", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["robustness", "conclusion"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [228]}, {"id": 230, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[269, 269]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 231, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[270, 270]], "note": "tool-output end tag"}]}}